## Repository Layout — Multi-Repo Wrapper

This root directory is a thin wrapper acting as the shared specs/documentation
repository. The subdirectories are **independent git repositories** with their own
remotes — always run git commands inside the subdirectory you changed, never at
the root:

- `{{BACKEND_DIR}}/` — {{BACKEND_STACK_SUMMARY}} (`{{BACKEND_REPO_URL}}`)
- `{{FRONTEND_DIR}}/` — {{FRONTEND_STACK_SUMMARY}} (`{{FRONTEND_REPO_URL}}`)

**All Claude Code sessions must be started from this wrapper root — never from
inside a sub-repo.** When implementing a feature, always confirm which repository
is active before changing files. See `docs/process/repository-strategy.md` for the
cross-repository feature rule (backend contract before frontend implementation).
